================================================================================
AUDIO FIXTURES
================================================================================

No audio fixtures are committed to this repository; they are fetched and derived
by the commands in `fixtures/asr/README.md`. This section documents their
provenance for anyone who does redistribute them.

`parity_jfk.wav` is fetched from whisper.cpp (`samples/jfk.wav`):
    https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
    Copyright (c) 2023-2024 The ggml authors
    Licence: MIT

Its content is an excerpt of John F. Kennedy's 1961 inaugural address, a work of
the United States federal government and therefore in the public domain
(17 U.S.C. Sec. 105).

`parity_short.wav` and `parity_long_quiet.wav` are **derived from that same
recording** by `fixtures/asr/make_fixtures.py` — not synthetic. `parity_short`
is its first 0.75 s; `parity_long_quiet` is the clip tiled to 130 s and
normalised to about -30 dBFS. Both inherit the provenance above.
